Title: fix(secrets): remove exposed keys from .env and add .env.example

Summary
- Removed plaintext secrets from `.env` and added `.env.example` with placeholders.
- Added `.gitignore` entry to ensure `.env` is not committed.
- Added guidance for rotation and history-purging in the PR template.

Files changed
- `.env` — removed real secret values (replaced with placeholder or removed file from index)
- `.env.example` — new (contains placeholders and explanatory comments)
- `.gitignore` — ensure `.env` is ignored (if not already)
- `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md` — added/updated to include secrets checklist

What I changed
- Removed these keys from the repo (examples found in the committed `.env`):
  - `GROQ_API_KEY`
  - `OPENAI_API_KEY`
  - `SMTP_PASSWORD` (and other SMTP credentials)
- Created `.env.example` with placeholders and short notes for each key.
- Added `.env` to `.gitignore` and removed `.env` from the index using `git rm --cached .env`.

Why
- Plaintext secrets were committed and are visible publicly; this is a security risk and must be remediated immediately.

Actions already taken in this branch
1. Removed secrets from the working tree and committed the removal.
2. Added `.env.example` with placeholders and explanatory comments.
3. Added/updated `.gitignore` to ignore `.env`.
4. Added PR template with a security checklist to help future contributors.

Required immediate post-merge actions (do not skip)
- [ ] Rotate the exposed keys in each provider console (OpenAI, Sanity/GROQ, SMTP provider, etc.).
- [ ] Update deployment/CI secrets with the new rotated values.
- [ ] If you need to purge secrets from git history, coordinate with all contributors and follow the purge guidance in the PR template (BFG recommended).

Optional: Purge history guidance (use with care)
```
# remove a file completely from history (example)
git filter-branch --force --index-filter "git rm --cached --ignore-unmatch .env" --prune-empty --tag-name-filter cat -- --all
# or use BFG Repo Cleaner: https://rtyley.github.io/bfg-repo-cleaner/
```
Note: Rewriting history requires everyone to re-clone or rebase their work. Rotate keys before or immediately after purging.

Suggested reviewers / owners
- @repo-owner
- @devops
- @security

Notes
- I created this branch as a Draft PR so the team can rotate keys and coordinate history changes before merging.
- I recommend rotating keys first, then optionally purging history if the secrets were present in older commits.

How to use this file
1. In the GitHub UI when creating the PR, copy the contents of this file and paste it into the PR description box.
2. Set the PR to Draft. Tag the suggested reviewers and ping the ops/security team to rotate keys.
